# Summoner's Grimoire ({3}{G} Equipment, job select; "Equipped creature is a Shaman in addition to its other types and has
# 'Whenever this creature attacks, you may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield. If that card is an
# enchantment card, it enters tapped and attacking.'"). Bot1 casts it off Black Lotus and Mox Emerald: job select makes a 1/1
# Hero Shaman it is attached to. On turn 3 the Hero attacks: Bot1 puts Enduring Vitality (an enchantment creature card) into
# play, tapped and attacking (Bot2 20 - 1 - 3 = 16) - Bot2's Ornithopters, the creature cards in its hand, are not
# touched (Bot2 plays nothing). On turn 5 the Hero and Vitality attack and Llanowar Elves, not an enchantment card, enters
# untapped and not attacking (Bot2 16 - 4 = 12; the Elves are in play, untapped). On turn 7 Bot1 declines to put the Ornithopter in
# its hand: it stays there (with the Forests drawn).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Black Lotus
Summoner's Grimoire
Enduring Vitality
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Forest
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Summoner's Grimoire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Hero Token.Subtypes = Hero; Shaman
? Bot1.Battlefield.Summoner's Grimoire.AttachedTo = Hero Token
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Hero Token > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Enduring Vitality)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Enduring Vitality.Tapped = true
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 16
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Hero Token > Bot2; Enduring Vitality > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Llanowar Elves)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 12
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Hero Token > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose()

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
